ment 2408\n\n--- Record 2334 ---\nComponent: Peppol Exchange\nEnvironment: Neo\nTitle: Mandatory migration from the Peppol Exchange service to SAP Document and Reporting Compliance, cloud edition\nDescription: The Peppol Exchange service for the cloud edition of SAP Document and Reporting Compliance (Neo environment) will no longer be available as of April 1, 2025. To continue exchanging electronic documents in the Peppol network, you must migrate to SAP Document and Reporting Compliance, cloud edition (multi-cloud foundation).      For more information about the new version, see SAP Document and Reporting Compliance, Cloud Edition.      For migration information, see Migrating to SAP Document and Reporting Compliance, Cloud Edition    \nAction: Required\nLifecycle: Deprecated\nType: Announcement\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-01-01\nValid as Of: 2024-08-30\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 2335 ---\nComponent: SAP Build Process Automation\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Create Scheduled Trigger to Start your Process\nDescription: You can create a scheduled trigger to start your process. In process editor, choose Add a Trigger and then choose Scheduled Trigger.  See Create a Scheduled Trigger to Start a Process.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-08-29\nValid as Of: 2024-08-29\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 2336 ---\nComponent: UI Theme Designer\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Belize is deprecated for theming\nDescription: It is time to migrate your custom theme based on Belize to a theme based on Horizon or Quartz. Some UI frameworks do not support Belize themes in their latest versions anymore. For example, SAPUI5 doesn't support Belize themes from 1.120 upwards, see Supported Combinations of Themes and Libraries for details. Themes based on a Belize theme will not run anymore for all UI frameworks. This is why using Belize themes as base for a custom theme is deprecated. If you have created a custom theme based on a Belize theme, please migrate your theme to a Horizon or Quartz theme. You find a how-to at Migrating Themes. Belize is removed for theming at the beginning of 2025.\nAction: Recommended\nLifecycle: Deprecated\nType: Announcement\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-01-01\nValid as Of: 2024-08-28\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 2337 ---\nComponent: Continuous Integration & Delivery\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: New Domain for Subscriptions\nDescription: New SAP Continuous Integration and Delivery subscriptions will use the domain cloud.sap.  This domain will be used by all SaaS applications offered by SAP to facilitate integration scenarios.  Existing subscriptions and bookmarks to ondemand.com will continue to work.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-08-28\nValid as Of: 2024-08-28\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 2338 ---\nComponent: SAP Build Process Automation\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Notifications\nDescription: You can stay updated and take timely action on a new task created using the Notifications feature. See   Enable Notifications  Manage and Personalize your Notifications  \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-08-28\nValid as Of: 2024-08-28\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 2339 ---\nComponent: Cloud Identity Services\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry,Kyma,Neo\nTitle: Regular Upgrade\nDescription: Cloud Identity Services have been upgraded.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision", ": General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-08-28\nValid as Of: 2024-08-28\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 2339 ---\nComponent: Cloud Identity Services\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry,Kyma,Neo\nTitle: Regular Upgrade\nDescription: Cloud Identity Services have been upgraded.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-08-27\nValid as Of: 2024-08-27\nVersion: 26573\n\n--- Record 2340 ---\nComponent: SAP Datasphere\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Features for Version 2024.18\nDescription: New and changed features are available for administration, data cataloging, data integration, data modeling, SAP BW Bridge, and space management.  For more information, see What's New in SAP Datasphere 2024.18. \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-08-27\nValid as Of: 2024-08-27\nVersion: Cloud\n\n", "--- Record 1261 ---\nComponent: Edge Integration Cell\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Customizable proxy settings enabled for the AS2 sender adapter\nDescription: You can now set the proxy type settings if you have Edge Integration Cell runtime activated.  For more information, see   Configure the AS2 Sender Adapter  Configure the AS2 Receiver Adapter      SAP Cloud Integration customers, see   Configure the AS2 Sender Adapter  Configure the AS2 Receiver Adapter  \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-03-09\nValid as Of: 2025-03-09\nVersion: 2501\n\n--- Record 1262 ---\nComponent: Edge Integration Cell\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Enhancements in the Diagnostics Tasks table\nDescription: New enhancements in the Diagnostic Tasks table include:  The new Table Settings allows you to show or hide additional columns and change their order in the table.  An additional column Component is available.  The overflow button contains the option Details, which opens a dialog showing details about the task.    See: Diagnostics\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-03-09\nValid as Of: 2025-03-09\nVersion: 2501\n\n--- Record 1263 ---\nComponent: Edge Integration Cell\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Kubernetes (K8s) 1.31. is now supported\nDescription: Edge Integration Cell now supports Kubernetes (K8s) 1.31.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-03-09\nValid as Of: 2025-03-09\nVersion: 2501\n\n--- Record 1264 ---\nComponent: Edge Integration Cell\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Software Version Update\nDescription:     Edge Integration Cell: 8.27.*    Increment: 2501  \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-03-09\nValid as Of: 2025-03-09\nVersion: 2501\n\n--- Record 1265 ---\nComponent: Edge Integration Cell\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Updates on Heap Dump Diagnostic Tasks\nDescription: New updates on the Heap Dump Diagnostic Task include:    You can now analyze heap dumps and download the analysis results instead of the raw heap dumps.   New statuses and actions are available.    See: Heap Dumps\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-03-09\nValid as Of: 2025-03-09\nVersion: 2501\n\n--- Record 1266 ---\nComponent: Event Mesh\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Specify parameters in JSON file when configuring a message client.\nDescription: You can specify parameters like namespace and connection rules for a messaging client. See Configure a Message Client.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-03-09\nValid as Of: 2025-03-09\nVersion: 2501\n\n--- Record 1267 ---\nComponent: Integration Assessment\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Software Version Update\nDescription:     Integration Assessment: 1.37.*      Increment: 2501    \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-03-09\nValid as Of: 2025-03-09\nVersion: 2501\n\n--- Record 1268 ---\nComponent: Migration Assessment\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Extended Evaluation of XSLT Mappings\nDescription: Rules have been added for analyzing usage of Java extensions and the number of dependencies in XLST mappings. This allows a more accurate estimate of the migration effort.  The additional information is reported in the full evaluation result spreadsheet. Please note that to view this new information, you will need to perform a new data extraction. For more details on how to extract the your data, visit Create a Data Extraction Request.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-03-09\nValid as Of: 2025-03-09\nVersion: 2501\n\n--- Record 1269 ---\nComponent: Migration Assessment\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Software Version Update\nDescription:     Migration Assessment: 1.37.*      Increment: 2501    \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-03-09\nValid as Of: 2025-03-09\nVersion: 2501\n\n--- Record 1270 ---\nComponent: SAP Business Application Studio\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Calculation Views\nDescription: In the calculation view editor, an execution hint is now available that lets you control the automatic removal of duplicate edges in hierarchies. This option can be accessed from the Select Execution Hint from List dialog.  See Supported Execution Hints.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-03-18\nValid as Of: 2025-03-09\nVersion: T2502a\n\n", "--- Record 1661 ---\nComponent: Cloud Portal Service\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Built-In Support\nDescription: Built-In Support is a support platform that enables you to get access to support content and channels directly from your current system.  To use this feature, enable it in the Site Settings screen. This displays a headset icon in the menu bar of the site.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-01-09\nValid as Of: 2025-01-09\nVersion: 2413A\n\n--- Record 1662 ---\nComponent: Connectivity\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Destination Service - New Authentication Type\nDescription: For HTTP destinations, a new authentication type OAuth2TokenExchange (based on RFC8693) is now available.  For more information, see OAuth Token Exchange Authentication.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-01-09\nValid as Of: 2025-01-09\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 1663 ---\nComponent: Connectivity\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry,Neo\nTitle: Java Connector 3.1.11.0 - Bug Fixes\nDescription: Release of Java Connector (JCo) version 3.1.11.0 provides the following bug fix:  When calling JCoRepository.load(java.io.Reader), the cache of the JCoRepository instance was not cleared, neither before reading the metadata nor if an error occurred during the load operation. Thus, previously cached function templates and record metadata as well as newly loaded metadata could have been rendered unusable. Working with such invalid or wrong metadata could have resulted in various follow-up errors like NullPointerExceptions or garbled content data.  This issue hass been fixed.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-01-09\nValid as Of: 2025-01-09\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 1664 ---\nComponent: Connectivity\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry,Neo\nTitle: Java Connector 3.1.11.0 - Enhancements\nDescription: Release of Java Connector (JCo) version 3.1.11.0 provides the following enhancement:  The new API com.sap.conn.jco.JCoRepository.isEmpty() has been added and is available for general use. See the API documentation for details.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-01-09\nValid as Of: 2025-01-09\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 1665 ---\nComponent: Document Management Service\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Recycle Bin Update\nDescription: With this release, the Recycle Bin includes additional features such as access control checks, deletion events, search, pagination, and folder path management. Please note that access to this feature depends on the level of access control granted to users.  See Using the Recycle Bin and Deleting and Restoring Files and Folders.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-01-09\nValid as Of: 2025-01-09\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 1666 ---\nComponent: Document Management Service\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: UI Improvements: Advanced Search\nDescription: We have updated the    Advanced Searchon the Document Management Service, Application Option UI with the following features:  Add and Remove Fields: Use the Filters option to customize your search fields.  Rearrange Fields: Organize search fields to suit your needs.  Search and Group Fields: Find and group fields easily using the Filters option.  Reset Filters: Quickly reset filters to start a new search.  \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-01-09\nValid as Of: 2025-01-09\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 1667 ---\nComponent: SAP BTP Cockpit\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry,Other\nTitle: Displaying Who Created and Last Modified Service Instances in the SAP BTP Cockpit\nDescription: We've added Created By and Modified By fields to the Instances and Subscriptions page of subaccounts and to the Service Instances page of Cloud Foundry spaces in the SAP BTP cockpit to show who created and modified service instances.  Note that the feature is now available for all three types of entities that can be created in SAP BTP cockpit: service instances, environment instances, and subscriptions.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-01-01\nValid as Of: 2025-01-09\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 1668 ---\nComponent: SAP BTP, Cloud Foundry Runtime\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Version 45.0.0\nDescription: Cloud Foundry has been updated from 44.9.0 to 45.0.0.      https://github.com/cloudfoundry/cf-deployment/releases/tag/v45.0.0  https://github.com/cloudfoundry/cf-deployment/releases/tag/v44.11.0  https://github.com/cloudfoundry/cf-deployment/releases/tag/v44.10.0    \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-01-09\nValid as Of: 2025-01-09", "ry/cf-deployment/releases/tag/v45.0.0  https://github.com/cloudfoundry/cf-deployment/releases/tag/v44.11.0  https://github.com/cloudfoundry/cf-deployment/releases/tag/v44.10.0    \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-01-09\nValid as Of: 2025-01-09\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 1669 ---\nComponent: SAP Build Work Zone, advanced edition\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Built-In Support\nDescription: Built-In Support is a support platform that enables you to get access to support content and channels directly from your current system.  To use this feature, enable it in the Site Settings screen. This displays a headset icon in the menu bar of the site.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-01-09\nValid as Of: 2025-01-09\nVersion: 2413A\n\n--- Record 1670 ---\nComponent: SAP Build Work Zone, standard edition\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Built-In Support\nDescription: Built-In Support is a support platform that enables you to get access to support content and channels directly from your current system.  To use this feature, enable it in the Site Settings screen. This displays a headset icon in the menu bar of the site.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-01-09\nValid as Of: 2025-01-09\nVersion: 2413A\n\n", "--- Record 2641 ---\nComponent: Forms Service by Adobe\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Availability - Additional Regions\nDescription: The SAP Forms service is now available in the following additional regions (Azure):    Europe - Netherleands (cf-eu20-001)  Switzerland - Zurich (cf-ch20 - EU access)    For more information, see also SAP Discovery Center.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Announcement\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-01-01\nValid as Of: 2024-07-09\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 2642 ---\nComponent: Forms Service by Adobe\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: New Features\nDescription: The SAP Forms service provides the following new features:     A new landing page lets you access the Forms service tools and UIs easily.For more information, see Forms Service Landing Page.  You can now create a Forms service template store repository manually.For more information, see Create a Template Store Repository.  \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-01-01\nValid as Of: 2024-07-09\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 2643 ---\nComponent: Kyma Runtime\nEnvironment: Kyma\nTitle: Keda module: Update to version 1.2.0\nDescription: In this release, we have updated the KEDA version to 2.14.0.  Additionally, we have introduced a dedicated priority class for the managed KEDA workloads, which prevents the eviction of the KEDA Pods in the resource-congested clusters.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-06-28\nValid as Of: 2024-07-09\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 2644 ---\nComponent: SAP Task Center\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Minor Improvements\nDescription: For enhanced performance, the removal of unused API has been finalized.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Announcement\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-07-09\nValid as Of: 2024-07-09\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 2645 ---\nComponent: SAP AI Core\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Generative AI hub\nDescription: Additional selected models from GCP Vertex AI are supported.  For more information, see SAP Note 3437766 .\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Announcement\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-07-08\nValid as Of: 2024-07-08\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 2646 ---\nComponent: SAP AI Launchpad\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Generative AI hub\nDescription: Additional selected models from GCP Vertex AI are supported.For more information, see Models and Scenarios in the Generative AI Hub.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-07-08\nValid as Of: 2024-07-08\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 2647 ---\nComponent: SAP Document AI\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Improved Extraction of Line Items Directly above Document Footers\nDescription: We’ve fixed an issue with the extraction of line items. If the line spacing between the final line item and the document footer is the same as the line spacing in the line items, SAP Document AI no longer extracts the footer text as part of the final line item.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Intelligent Technologies\nLatest Revision: 2024-07-08\nValid as Of: 2024-07-08\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 2648 ---\nComponent: SAP Document AI\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Schema Description and Schema Field Description\nDescription: We’ve increased the maximum length of the following strings to 500 characters:  schemaDescription  schema field description    See Create Schema and Add Fields to Schema Version.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Intelligent Technologies\nLatest Revision: 2024-07-08\nValid as Of: 2024-07-08\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 2649 ---\nComponent: Credential Store\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry,Kyma\nTitle: CMK Encryption Details\nDescription: You can now view the encryption details of your customer-managed keys (CMK) in the SAP Credential Store user interface See:       Customer-Managed Keys (CMK)      View CMK Encryption Details    \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-06-28\nValid as Of: 2024-07-05\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 2650 ---\nComponent: Object Store\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry,Kyma\nTitle: Role-based service bindings on AWS\nDescription: Object Store Service now supports read and write role based service binding credentials. Please refer the section Role-based Bindings and Service-keys for more details.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-07-04\nValid as Of: 2024-07-04\nVersion: Cloud\n\n", "--- Record 3711 ---\nComponent: Continuous Integration & Delivery\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Deprecation of Chromium Versions Lower than version 115\nDescription: WebdriverIO tests that use a Chromium version lower than 115 will no longer be supported by SAP Continuous Integration and Delivery after March 31th, 2024. Instead, we recommended to use latest for chromdedriver version in the associated package.json file.\nAction: Recommended\nLifecycle: Deprecated\nType: Announcement\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2023-12-19\nValid as Of: 2023-12-19\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 3712 ---\nComponent: Continuous Integration & Delivery\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Automatic Detection of Chromium Version\nDescription: SAP Continuous Integration and Delivery now automatically detects which chromedriver version to use. Therefore, the version set in the package.json file associated with your job is not necessarily taken into account, but rather the Chromium version that is available in the environment. We recommend to use latest for chromdedriver version in the package.json file.  To use this feature in your local development, add the property detect_chromedriver_version=true in a .npmrc file.\nAction: Recommended\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2023-12-19\nValid as Of: 2023-12-19\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 3713 ---\nComponent: Cloud Identity Services\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry,Kyma,Neo\nTitle: Custom Mail Server\nDescription: Tenant administrator can configure rate limits per minute for the emails. See Configure Custom Mail Server.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2023-12-19\nValid as Of: 2023-12-19\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 3714 ---\nComponent: Cloud Identity Services\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry,Kyma,Neo\nTitle: Regular Upgrade\nDescription: Identity Authentication has been upgraded.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2023-12-19\nValid as Of: 2023-12-19\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 3715 ---\nComponent: Cloud Identity Services\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry,Kyma,Neo\nTitle: Regular Upgrade\nDescription: Identity Authentication has been upgraded.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2023-12-19\nValid as Of: 2023-12-19\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 3716 ---\nComponent: Cloud Identity Services\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry,Kyma,Neo\nTitle: User Attributes for Subscribed Applications\nDescription: Tenant administrator can enable or disable the attribute mappings inherited from the subscribed multitenant applications. See Configuring User Attributes from a Corporate Identity Provider.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2023-12-19\nValid as Of: 2023-12-19\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 3717 ---\nComponent: Continuous Integration & Delivery\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Added Node 20 Build Tool Version\nDescription: The Node 20 build tool version now is available for pure Node.js projects as well as for Cloud MTA Build Tool (MBT) projects together with Java 11 or Java 17.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2023-12-19\nValid as Of: 2023-12-19\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 3718 ---\nComponent: Continuous Integration & Delivery\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Credential List Configuration\nDescription: For jobs that are configured in the Source Repository configuration mode, as an administrator, you can now configure credential lists to specify the credentials that are passed to the build. See (Optional) Configure a Credential List.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2023-12-19\nValid as Of: 2023-12-19\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 3719 ---\nComponent: Continuous Integration & Delivery\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Export of Transport Requests to SAP Cloud ALM\nDescription: Transport requests can now be directly exported to SAP Cloud ALM by providing an SAP Cloud ALM service key.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2023-12-19\nValid as Of: 2023-12-19\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 3720 ---\nComponent: Identity Provisioning\nEnvironment: Neo\nTitle: Renamed System\nDescription: The SAP S/4HANA Cloud for advanced financial closing connector has been renamed to SAP Advanced Financial Closing.  For more information, see: SAP Advanced Financial Closing\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2023-12-06\nValid as Of: 2023-12-19\nVersion: Cloud\n\n", "--- Record 1861 ---\nComponent: SAP BTP Command Line Interface\nEnvironment: ABAP,Cloud Foundry,Kyma,Neo,Other\nTitle: Deprecation of btp CLI Client Versions 2.54 through 2.61\nDescription: All client versions up until and including 2.61 have been deprecated. These versions will no longer work after June 30, 2025.  Action: If you're still using one of these versions, you need to update to the latest btp CLI client version. See Download and Start Using the btp CLI Client.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Announcement\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-11-26\nValid as Of: 2024-11-28\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 1862 ---\nComponent: SAP BTP Command Line Interface\nEnvironment: ABAP,Cloud Foundry,Kyma,Neo,Other\nTitle: Expansion of the btp CLI Command Autocompletion Feature\nDescription: The btp CLI command autocompletion feature has been expanded to include client commands (such as login and target), as well as command options. See Enable Command Autocompletion.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-11-26\nValid as Of: 2024-11-28\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 1863 ---\nComponent: SAP BTP, Cloud Foundry Runtime\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Version 44.5.0\nDescription: Cloud Foundry has been updated from 44.3.0 to 44.5.0.      https://github.com/cloudfoundry/cf-deployment/releases/tag/v44.5.0  https://github.com/cloudfoundry/cf-deployment/releases/tag/v44.4.0    \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-11-28\nValid as Of: 2024-11-28\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 1864 ---\nComponent: SAP Build Apps\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Web & Mobile\nDescription: To improve the user experience, we have updated the navigation menu in the global toolbar. App developers now have access to the Variables directly from the menu. The previous UI Canvas and Data tabs are now renamed respectively to User Interface and Integrations. To save space, the less frequently used Theme, Navigation, Authentication and Help options are now grouped under the App Settings drop-down menu. In the upper right corner, you can access the Preview button. Next to it is the Publish button, which enables you either to Create a Release Version or to Build and Deploy.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-11-28\nValid as Of: 2024-11-28\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 1865 ---\nComponent: SAP Secure Login Service\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: sncForceLogin Parameter\nDescription: You can now enforce a reauthentication whenever the end user opens a SAP GUI connection. You can configure this by setting the sncForceLogin parameter, which is a local policy property. For more information, see Profile Settings.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-11-28\nValid as Of: 2024-11-28\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 1866 ---\nComponent: SAPUI5\nEnvironment: ABAP,Cloud Foundry,Kyma,Neo,Other\nTitle: SAPUI5 Distribution 1.131\nDescription: SAPUI5 version 1.131 has been released for UI development and can now be consumed by SAP BTP services. It’s up to the services to determine when they start using the new version.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Announcement\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-11-27\nValid as Of: 2024-11-28\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 1867 ---\nComponent: Service Manager\nEnvironment: ABAP,Cloud Foundry,Kyma,Other\nTitle: REST API\nDescription: We've added \"Created By\" and \"Modified By\" fields to the Service Manager APIs for service instances and service binding GET responses. See Service Manager API.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-11-19\nValid as Of: 2024-11-28\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 1868 ---\nComponent: Kyma Runtime\nEnvironment: Kyma\nTitle: API Gateway module: Update to version 2.9.0\nDescription: This release introduces support for the path operators {*} and {**} in the APIRule v2alpha1 custom resource. The {*} operator (for example, /foo/{*} or /foo/{*}/bar) matches any request with exactly one path segment in the operator’s place. The {**} operator (for example, /foo/{**}  or /foo/{**}/bar) matches any request with zero or more path segments in the operator’s place. {**} must be the last operator in the path. For more information, see APIRule v2alpha1 Specification.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-11-13\nValid as Of: 2024-11-27\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 186", "  or /foo/{**}/bar) matches any request with zero or more path segments in the operator’s place. {**} must be the last operator in the path. For more information, see APIRule v2alpha1 Specification.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-11-13\nValid as Of: 2024-11-27\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 1869 ---\nComponent: Kyma Runtime\nEnvironment: Kyma\nTitle: Kyma service binding\nDescription: We are excited to introduce a new feature, Kyma service binding, which enables automatic management of a Kyma instance. With this feature, you can access a Kyma cluster, deploy applications, run tests, and delete resources in a fully automated manner.  For more information, see Managing Kyma Runtime Using the Provisioning Service API.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-11-28\nValid as Of: 2024-11-27\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 1870 ---\nComponent: Multitarget Applications for Cloud Foundry\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: New restriction regarding the size of deployments in transport scenarios via cTMS or CTS+\nDescription: The maximum size of deployments which use multiple MTA archives should be no more than 20GB. This restriction is applicable only in transport scenarios via cTMS or CTS+, where one transport request with multiple MTAs results in a single deployment process in SAP Cloud Deployment service.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-11-18\nValid as Of: 2024-11-27\nVersion: Cloud\n\n"], "parameters": {"model": "text-embedding-3-small"}}, "key": "embeddings_4e61a14d24dcaa47d583a4e64ff3b73c199f4c60e6f27812587832bdf52a84ac_v2"}